{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1535082","title":"Detection and characterization of Vibrio parahaemolyticus recovered from some wastewater systems in South Africa: A One Health perspective","description":"Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is an increasing global public health challenge driven by the widespread misuse of antibiotics and the environmental dissemination of antimicrobial resistant microorganisms and antimicrobial resistance genes (ARGs). Wastewater treatment plants (WWTPs) serve as critical reservoirs for antibiotic-resistant bacteria (ARB) and ARGs, due to the inflow of influent from various sources (including hospitals), with many studies reporting municipal WWTPs facilitating ARG persistence and spread into the environment. This study investigated the occurrence and antibiogram characteristics of Vibrio parahaemolyticus isolated from selected WWTPs in the Eastern Cape Province, within the One Health framework.","center":"University of the Witwatersrand","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/09/25 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN63554577","Vibrio parahaemolyticus  53","uncertain",null,"2025-09-03",2025,"ZA","Eastern Cape",1009863,"Dimbaza","verified",null,null,"South Africa: Eastern Cape, Dimbaza","Wastewater treatment plant",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN63554578","Vibrio parahaemolyticus  55","uncertain",null,"2025-09-03",2025,"ZA","Eastern Cape",1009863,"Dimbaza","verified",null,null,"South Africa: Eastern Cape, Dimbaza","Wastewater treatment plant",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN63554579","Vibrio parahaemolyticus  67","uncertain",null,"2025-09-03",2025,"ZA","Eastern Cape",null,null,"unresolv